    solid NxN blocks (N=3-5) arranged in a regular grid inside frame with 1-cell bg gaps
    grid: 2-3 rows x 3-4 cols; 0-2 cells may be empty
    total count: 6-10 blocks using 2-5 distinct placeholder colors
    each color appears 1+ times; all instances same NxN size
  sprites:
    one per placeholder color, placed outside frame, same NxN bbox as placeholders
    fill ratio: 0.50-0.90; may be 4-disconnected within bbox
    each sprite uses only its placeholder color + bg
  legends:
    one per placeholder color, fixed 3x4 pattern outside frame, no bg in the 3x4 block
    pattern: |
      src src tgt tgt
      src src src tgt
      src src tgt tgt
    src = placeholder color (area 7), tgt = output color (area 5)
    src determined by: if exactly one color is a placeholder, that is src; else larger-area component is src
    tgt colors may overlap with placeholder colors or be entirely new
  output:
    the frame region only; interior has placeholders replaced by sprites recolored to legend-mapped tgt color
    frame border preserved; interior bg cells stay bg

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose bg, frame_col (5), N (3-5), grid dims R x C (2-3 x 3-4), 0-2 empty cells
    2. Choose K = number of placeholder colors (2-5), assign distinct placeholder colors and tgt colors
    3. Generate K random NxN sprites (fill 50-90%, connected or not, at least 1 bg cell)
    4. Build output frame interior: place sprites (recolored to tgt) on the RxC grid with 1-bg-gap, empty cells stay bg
    5. Build input frame interior: replace each sprite region with a solid NxN block of its placeholder color
    6. Place frame border around the interior
    7. Place K legend blocks (3x4 fixed pattern) outside frame with bg gaps
    8. Place K sprite templates (original placeholder-colored NxN) outside frame, separated by bg from legends/frame
    9. Pad to final grid size with bg; ensure all outside elements fit without overlap
